course: dictionary
lesson: 5578
title: The Levant: a place and a rare word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Levant is the name of a region, a large area of land, not one single country. Context clues help you find out where it is. «Dabke is a line dance from the Levant, including Lebanon, Syria, Palestine and Jordan, with linked hands and stamping feet.» The sentence lists countries, so the Levant must be a region that contains them.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: "Dabke is a line dance from the lands on the eastern shore of the Mediterranean." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Some words hide in old slang. Levant can also be a verb, but this is old UK slang and very rare. To levant meant to run away without paying your debts. When you meet a rare word in an old story, do not guess wildly. Look it up in a dictionary.
fact: The Levant is an old name for the lands on the eastern shore of the Mediterranean Sea.
fact: Today the Levant mainly means Lebanon, Syria, Israel, Palestine and Jordan, and sometimes Cyprus and parts of Turkey.
fact: The name comes from French «lever», meaning to rise, because the sun rises in the east.
fact: Food from the Levant, like hummus and falafel, is called Levantine.
fact: To levant is old, rare UK slang meaning to run away without paying your debts.
exercise: «Dabke is a line dance from the Levant, with linked hands and stamping feet.» What is the Levant? | A kind of stamping shoe | A large dance hall in a city | *A region on the eastern shore of the Mediterranean Sea
exercise: The name Levant comes from French «lever», meaning to rise. Why is it named that? | Because many people there rise early to work | *Because the sun rises in the east | Because the land is very high above the sea
exercise: Hummus and falafel come from the Levant. What kind of food are they called? | *Levantine | Australian | Dutch | Scottish
test: Which of these is an old, rare word meaning to run away without paying your debts? | Levantine | falafel | dabke | *levant
test: Which countries are mainly in the Levant today? | *Lebanon, Syria, Israel, Palestine and Jordan | Canada and Mexico | Scotland, Wales and Ireland | Spain, France and Italy
exam: Jayden reads «the countries of the Levant» in a history book and does not know the word. What should he do first? | Ignore it, because words never matter | *Read the clues around it: the phrase names a region, so look for the countries it lists | Guess it is the name of a famous king | Skip the whole book and never return to it
